From b8462be3369e3cd0f9bf04c4416b122bba7df27b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:23:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FieldOperations: end of time step on arrays of the calling
 code

- FieldOperations interface (copy and fill of views), with checks in the
  public non-virtual functions, as std::pmr::memory_resource.
  HostFieldOperations works in the memory of the host.
- Header-only implementations for CUDA, HIP, SYCL, Kokkos and OpenMP
  offloading in MGIS/FieldOperations, compiled by the calling code.
- update, revert and updateValues of material data managers and views
  take operations: the values held by MGIS are updated on the host, the
  arrays of the calling code by the operations. Mixed copies are refused
  if the location is not accessible by the host.
- Empty views have distinct values (empty groups of variables).
- CUDA test: full cycle on device memory, compared to the host.
